Z||000015||phillip||05-26-2000||09:32 AM||||at the risk of beating a dead (sick?...tired? ) horse, i'll argue it again. a while back we were discussing a mistake sport compact car mag. (june 2000) made refering to fieros in a mr2 article. i sent an e- mail to correct them and took the opportunity to ask about a fiero article and /or build up. knowing that their not really into the v-8 thing i suggested maybe exploring a modern v6 (sc3800 or 4 cam) build up. they e-mailed back and said they'd consider it.<P>so it wasn't really a petition. i was saying with the number of people on the forum that will post for lesser reasons (the recent egr "discussion" comes to mind), if more people e-mailed them to show that there were more than one or two people interested ( a couple of other people said they had done the same thing but it was always a one or two person effort) it might sway their thinking.<P>i even mentioned that vendors could e-mail and offer their services/products. it seems to me have a least one major mag. (super street, probaly not unless you stick a honda engine in it) thinking about us could only help (except for maybe driving up prices it they got more popular). think of the products you've wished someone made for fieros. if vendors thought they had buyers they'd have more chance of being made.<P>ok, so i got my stick out and hit the horse one more time. it just seems like the effort involved in sending an e-mail is so minimal for the posible results gained.||||reg||1
